  "note": "A Bn defending a BUA by a number of localities of limited size, each held by a Coy, infiltration between them accepted (IBB S58 para 1 b p 319; IC s82 para 1 b pp 439-440): A and B Coys on the main routes in, C Coy in depth, D Coy the central mobile reserve (paras 3 h, 13 pp 322, 324); a Pl screen on the outer perimeter to deceive and contest the En first footholds (para 3 c pp 320-321); strong points in the strongest large buildings, mutually supporting and in depth; barricades, wire and mines on the main streets covered by their fire (para 3 g pp 321-322). Each locality drawn 400 x 300 m (bua.locality, E): 'of a limited size' with no figure printed (IC s52 para 1 c p 203), three Pl blocks whose fields of fire are about 50-100 m (IC s52 para 4 a (3) p 204), mutual support only within a Pl (IC s51 para 5 a (3) p 200); the Localities row warns past bua.localityMaxM, and on the ground a locality mostly outside the built-up area warns. The RRs on the periphery covering the tankable approaches and the street crossings, a tank Tp with a Coy on the edge (IC s57 paras 4 b-c, 12 a pp 238-240). Reinforcing a locality is often better than a counter-attack here (para 12 p 324).",
